Weather App – Python + OpenWeather API

A simple and user-friendly Weather Application built using Python (Flask) for the backend and HTML, CSS for the frontend.
This app fetches real-time weather data from the OpenWeatherMap API and displays temperature, humidity, wind speed, and weather conditions for any city entered by the user.

Features:

🌍 Search weather by city name

☁️ Real-time weather data using OpenWeatherMap API

🌡️ Displays temperature, humidity, wind speed & condition

🎨 Clean and responsive UI with HTML & CSS

🔗 Frontend integrated with Python backend using Flask

Tech Stack:

Frontend: HTML, CSS

Backend: Python (Flask)

API: OpenWeatherMap

Use Case:
Perfect for beginners learning API integration, frontend-backend connectivity, and Python web development.
